---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Projects | Jacob A. Torres"
  description="Machine learning, web development, and data analysis projects by Jacob A. Torres."
>
  <h1>Projects</h1>

  <p>
    I graduated from BloomTech (formerly Bloom Institute of Technology), where I
    studied full-stack web development, data engineering, and machine learning,
    and I'm currently completing my Bachelor's degree in Data Science and
    Machine Learning, with a minor in Linguistics, at Metropolitan State
    University of Denver. I spent a year at Scheduler.ai, an AI-driven
    scheduling platform, where I served as the lead full-stack web developer and
    contributed to the product's machine learning features. Primarily I am a
    Python developer, and I'm equally at home building accessible interfaces
    with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript/TypeScript.
  </p>

  <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Project sections">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#data-science">Data Science</a></li>
      <li><a href="#web-development">Web Development</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <section aria-labelledby="data-science">
    <h2 id="data-science">Data Science</h2>

    <p>
      I'm experienced with Python data science tools, Kaggle competitions and
      Jupyter notebooks, statistical analysis, and building data engineering ETL
      pipelines. Below are the models I've built, and a write-up of an analysis
      of federal housing data.
    </p>

    <ul class="project-list" aria-label="Data science projects">
      <li class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Machine Learning</span>
        <h3>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/jacob-torres/Spotify-Song-Suggester"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Spotify Song Suggester
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          A machine learning application which uses a neural network to generate
          a Spotify playlist based on a single song.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/projects/spotify-song-suggester">Read the write-up &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Machine Learning</span>
        <h3>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/jacob-torres/AirBnB-Optimal-Price"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Airbnb Optimal Price
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          A Flask web application which calculates the optimal price to rent an
          Airbnb property using machine learning.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/projects/airbnb-optimal-price">Read the write-up &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="teaser">
      <h3 id="housing-the-homeless">Housing the Homeless</h3>
      <p class="article-subtitle">
        Does investing in permanent housing for the homeless significantly
        decrease homelessness?
      </p>
      <p class="article-date">
        <time datetime="2020-10-25">October 25, 2020</time>
      </p>

      <p>
        I analyzed the most recent available data on homelessness in the United
        States, collected and provided by the Department of Housing and Urban
        Development (HUD), to ask whether a state's investment in permanent
        supportive housing significantly decreases the number of homeless people
        in that state.
      </p>

      <p>
        Comparing point-in-time counts against housing inventory counts from
        2007 to 2019, the states that invested most heavily in permanent
        supportive housing were the states where homelessness fell, and an
        independent t-test put the result below the 0.05 significance level.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/projects/housing-the-homeless"
          >Read the full analysis &rarr;</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="web-development">
    <h2 id="web-development">Web Development</h2>

    <p>
      I build web applications with Django and Flask, and I'm skilled in
      accessible UI development with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript/TypeScript. Below
      are some of my web development projects, including deployed sites you can
      visit live.
    </p>

    <ul class="project-list" aria-label="Web development projects">
      <li class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Web Development</span>
        <h3>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/jacob-torres/story-builder"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Story Builder
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          A web application for collaboratively writing and organizing short
          fiction and stories.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Live Site</span>
        <h3>
          <a
            href="https://jacob-torres.github.io/Denver-Streets"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Denver Street Guide
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          An operations and maintenance street reference guide for the Denver
          metro area.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="project-card">
        <span class="tag">Live Site</span>
        <h3>
          <a
            href="https://denver-nav.onrender.com"
            rel="external noopener"
          >
            Accessible Denver Navigation App
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          An accessible navigation application for getting around the Denver
          metro area.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
